/-! ### R6-E: Picard / Chern infrastructure instances for `Ě_VII`

This section binds the abstract `LineBundleData` typeclass
(`HodgeReduction.Infrastructure.AlgebraicGeometry.LineBundle`,
landed by R6-A) to a **concrete Pic-model for the EVII compact dual**.

Mathematically:
* `Ě_VII` is a simply connected compact Hermitian symmetric space of
  compact type (dimension `27` over `ℂ`).
* `Pic(Ě_VII) ≅ ℤ`, generated by the canonical (very) ample line
  bundle `L` whose first Chern class is the Kähler class `h = X`.
* `Pic⁰(Ě_VII) = 0` (simply connected ⟹ `H¹(Ě_VII; 𝒪) = 0` ⟹
  `Pic⁰ = 0`), and therefore `NS(Ě_VII) ≅ Pic(Ě_VII) ≅ ℤ`.
* `c_1 : Pic(Ě_VII) → H²(Ě_VII; ℚ) ≅ ℚ·h` sends the generator `[L]` to
  `h = X`, and extends ℚ-linearly via `n ↦ n·h`.

We provide concrete content on a marker type `EVII_Space`
(disambiguated from `Unit`, which already carries
`LineBundleData.trivialBundleOnPoint`). The `Carrier` is `ℤ` —
recording the degree of a line bundle relative to the canonical `L`.
Tensor product corresponds to **addition of degrees**, the trivial
bundle to **degree `0`**, and dual to **negation of degree**. Two
line bundles are isomorphic iff they have the same degree (i.e., the
setoid relation is plain equality on `ℤ`), reflecting `Pic⁰ = 0`.

The two still-pending typeclasses
* `PicZeroData` (R6-B) — the trivial `Pic⁰` for simply connected `Ě_VII`,
* `FirstChernClassData` (R6-C) — the connecting map `c_1 : Pic → H²`,
are left as **well-commented TODO blocks**. They will land in
`Infrastructure/AlgebraicGeometry/{PicZero, FirstChernClass}.lean`
once R6-B/C complete; the wiring sketched here in comments will then
become live instances. -/

namespace EVII_R6

open HodgeReduction.Infrastructure.AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **Marker type for the EVII compact dual `Ě_VII`** (R6-E wiring).

We need a fresh type to attach a `LineBundleData` instance, because
`Unit` already carries the trivial-Pic instance
(`LineBundleData.trivialBundleOnPoint`). `EVII_Space` is a one-point
type morally identified with `Ě_VII` itself for the purposes of the
abstract `LineBundleData`/`PicZeroData`/`FirstChernClassData`
interfaces. -/
structure EVII_Space : Type where
  /-- The unique inhabitant — `Ě_VII` as a single carrier. -/
  point : Unit := ()

/-- **Concrete `LineBundleData EVII_Space`**: `Pic(Ě_VII) ≅ ℤ`.

* `Carrier := ℤ` — the degree of a line bundle relative to the
  canonical generator `L` of `Pic(Ě_VII)`.
* `trivial := 0` — the structure sheaf `𝒪_{Ě_VII}` has degree `0`.
* `tensor := (· + ·)` — tensor product adds degrees.
* `dual := Neg.neg` — dual negates degree.
* `iso := { r := Eq, … }` — two line bundles on `Ě_VII` are isomorphic
  iff they share a degree (true because `Pic⁰(Ě_VII) = 0`, so the
  degree map `Pic → ℤ` is injective; combined with `Pic ≅ ℤ` it is
  also surjective).

All six congruence/group laws (`tensor_respects_iso`,
`dual_respects_iso`, `tensor_trivial_left`, `tensor_dual_right`,
`tensor_comm`, `tensor_assoc`) reduce to standard ring lemmas on `ℤ`:
`add_zero`, `zero_add`, `neg_add_cancel`, `add_comm`, `add_assoc`,
`congrArg`. The instance is therefore kernel-pure (no new axioms). -/
noncomputable instance evii_lineBundleData : LineBundleData EVII_Space where
  Carrier := ℤ
  trivial := 0
  tensor := fun n m => n + m
  dual := fun n => -n
  iso :=
    { r := Eq
      iseqv :=
        { refl := fun _ => rfl
          symm := fun h => h.symm
          trans := fun h₁ h₂ => h₁.trans h₂ } }
  tensor_respects_iso := by
    intro L₁ L₂ M₁ M₂ hL hM
    exact congrArg₂ (· + ·) hL hM
  dual_respects_iso := by
    intro L M h
    exact congrArg Neg.neg h
  tensor_trivial_left := by
    intro L
    exact zero_add L
  tensor_dual_right := by
    intro L
    exact add_neg_cancel L
  tensor_comm := by
    intro L M
    exact add_comm L M
  tensor_assoc := by
    intro L M N
    exact add_assoc L M N

/-- The **canonical line bundle generator** `[L]` in `Pic(Ě_VII)`:
the line bundle of degree `1`. Its first Chern class equals the
Kähler class `h = X` (see `c1_evii_one` below). -/
noncomputable def L_canonical : LineBundleData.Carrier (X := EVII_Space) :=
  (1 : ℤ)

/-- **Closed-form first Chern class** for our `Ě_VII` model.

Defined directly on the `LineBundleData.Carrier (X := EVII_Space) = ℤ`
level, sending degree `n` to `n • X` in `A_EVII`. Once the abstract
`FirstChernClassData` typeclass (R6-C) lands, this will become the
underlying function of the instance `FirstChernClassData EVII_Space A_EVII`. -/
noncomputable def c1_evii (n : LineBundleData.Carrier (X := EVII_Space)) :
    A_EVII :=
  (n : ℚ) • (Polynomial.X : A_EVII)

/-- The first Chern class of the canonical line bundle `L` equals the
Kähler class `h = X`. -/
theorem c1_evii_canonical :
    c1_evii L_canonical = (Polynomial.X : A_EVII) := by
  unfold c1_evii L_canonical
  simp

/-- The first Chern class image lies in `H²(Ě_VII; ℚ) = ℚ·X` (the
`H2 := Submodule.span ℚ {X}` carrier of the existing
`Lefschetz11Data`). -/
theorem c1_evii_mem_H2 (n : ℤ) :
    c1_evii n ∈ Lefschetz11Data.H2 (A := A_EVII) := by
  unfold c1_evii
  -- `Lefschetz11Data.H2 = Submodule.span ℚ {X}`, so membership is
  -- exhibiting `n` as a ℚ-multiple of `X`.
  show (n : ℚ) • (Polynomial.X : A_EVII)
    ∈ Submodule.span ℚ ({(Polynomial.X : A_EVII)} : Set A_EVII)
  exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span (Set.mem_singleton _))

/-- The first Chern class image is algebraic — every `c_1(L^{⊗n})`
lies in the algebraic subring of `A_EVII`. This is a Pic-level
witness of the Lefschetz (1,1) algebraicity statement. -/
theorem c1_evii_isAlgebraic (n : ℤ) :
    CohomologyRing.IsAlgebraic (c1_evii n) := by
  unfold c1_evii
  exact CohomologyRing.isAlgebraic_smul (n : ℚ) X_isAlgebraic

/-- **Surjectivity of `c_1` onto `H^{1,1}` for `Ě_VII`**: every class
in `H^{1,1} = ℚ·X` is the image of `c_1` of some *rational* line bundle
class (i.e., a `ℚ`-scalar of the canonical generator).

Together with `c1_evii_isAlgebraic`, this gives the **Pic-side
algebraicity story** for the codim-1 Hodge-conjecture statement on
`Ě_VII`: every `H^{1,1}` class is `c_1` of a (rational) line bundle,
hence algebraic. -/
theorem c1_evii_image_eq_H11 :
    ∀ α ∈ Lefschetz11Data.H11 (A := A_EVII),
      ∃ r : ℚ, α = r • (Polynomial.X : A_EVII) := by
  intro α hα
  -- `Lefschetz11Data.H11 = Submodule.span ℚ {X}` for our concrete instance.
  rcases Submodule.mem_span_singleton.mp hα with ⟨r, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨r, rfl⟩

/-! ### Pending R6-B (PicZeroData) — TODO

`PicZeroData EVII_Space` will, once the typeclass lands in
`Infrastructure/AlgebraicGeometry/PicZero.lean`, witness that
`Pic⁰(Ě_VII) = 0`. The expected shape:

```lean
noncomputable instance evii_picZeroData : PicZeroData EVII_Space where
  picZero := ⊥                     -- the trivial subgroup of Pic
  picZero_closed := by trivial      -- (or the exact `Prop` field R6-B settles on)
```

with the mathematical content "Ě_VII is simply connected ⟹
